    {
      "text": "You can use an IP address object to group and manage static IP addresses and subnets under a single name. To learn more about IP address objects, see About IP Address Objects."
    },
    {
      "text": "To configure an IP address object:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Private Access > VPN (for Legacy Apps) > VPN Access Policy IP Address.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          75
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Add Rule.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The Add IP Address Object page appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          25
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Add IP Address Object page:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          28
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "IP Address: Enter an IP address, and click Add. A maximum of 64 IP addresses or IP subnets is allowed. You can also click Import LAN/Client Subnets to define destinations from a predefined list.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ],
        [
          43,
          46
        ],
        [
          122,
          147
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Name: Enter name of the IP address object.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          4
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Save.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
